------------------------------------\
1) Build \'97 screens and behaviour\
------------------------------------\
\
1.1 Build workspace layout\
The Build workspace has three panes on one screen, look and feel like Cursor agent dashboard:\
- Chat pane (left): prompt box, file/link upload, history of messages and plans.\
- Content pane (centre): live Module core (sections, key points, source map) and generated lessons/checks (read while agent writes; editable when unlocked). **Each section and item shows provenance badges** (Internal, Certified Core, Industry source, Cerply templates).\
- Calibration pane (right): example items at different difficulty with reasons shown.\
User can reconfigure position and sizes of panes.\
\
1.2 Start a module\
- From Chat, a user can:\
  a) Type a content\uc0\u8209 first prompt, for example:\
     "Create a **Module core** called 'Trade Capture Fundamentals'.\
     **Audience:** new trade capture analysts in a global investment bank (basic Excel skills, no prior banking roles).\
     **Scope (in):** front\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 back trade flow for vanilla rates and FX; booking controls; key data fields; common breaks; UK/EU regulatory touchpoints (MiFID reporting high level).\
     **Scope (out):** exotic products; non\uc0\u8209 UK/EU rules; audit deep dives.\
     **Outcomes:** explain lifecycle; book a vanilla trade correctly; identify/escalate common breaks; interpret key booking fields.\
     **Sources:** attached onboarding deck; SOP_TradeBooking_v3.pdf; wiki links A/B. Web allowed for generic definitions only (Investopedia, BIS).\
     **Definitions:** include glossary (UTI, LEI, MTM).\
     **Edge cases:** partial fills; late trades; cancel/replace.\
     **Tone:** plain English; short sentences; include worked examples.\
     **Deliver:** core sections with key points and citations; one worked example per section; a short glossary; guidance notes where helpful. Generate **sample lessons/checks for Calibration only** \'97 the final Module assignment will be set later in Push."\
  b) Upload files or paste links.\
- \'93Prompt\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 Module\'94 creates a Module outline (title, goals, sections) and a short plan.\
- The agent proposes: Module title, goals, section outline, and initial **sample lessons/checks for Calibration**. **Delivery (channel, cadence, number of items) is defined later when creating a Module assignment in Push.** The user accepts or edits.\
\
1.3 Draft loop\
- After the outline is accepted, the agent drafts the Module core (sections, key points, citations) and then generates lessons and quick checks from that core into the Content pane.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - The agent **merges inputs** from prompts, uploads, Certified Core, and allowed industry sources into one coherent Module core.\
- **Duplicates are removed** and **conflicts are flagged** with side\uc0\u8209 by\u8209 side source excerpts so the user can resolve them.\
\pard\tqr\tx100\tx260\li260\fi-260\partightenfactor0
\cf2 	-	The agent uses the model orchestrator:\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li260\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95 Outline and Module core drafting run on a top model and include citations.\
\'95 A second top model runs a quality check for facts and citations (hallucination protection).\
\'95 Chat and small edits run on a small fast model for speed.\
\pard\tqr\tx100\tx260\li260\fi-260\partightenfactor0
\cf2 	-	If the quality check fails, the draft is flagged. The system will not lock the Module until the flags are fixed.\cf0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\sl340\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - New content derived from client uploads/prompts is marked **Internal** and saved to the client\'92s **Content Library**; external facts remain as citations (no bulk copying beyond fair\uc0\u8209 use extracts).\
- The Content pane shows a lock state while the agent writes. A banner reads \'93Agent is writing. You can read but not edit.\'94\
- When unlocked, the user edits and presses Send to apply edits. Conflicts show a warning with the option to merge or retry.\
- Calibration shows example Micro-Lessons and Quick Checks, generated from the module content, at different difficulty levels. A user can select an example and click \'93Add to chat\'94 to steer tone, length, or level. Items refresh each time the Content pane is refreshed.\
\
- The agent may read: Certified Core (read\uc0\u8209 only), **Cerply Building Blocks** (structure\u8209 only templates and patterns; no domain facts), client private library, and **allowed industry sources** (if permitted by client rules and filters).\
- When both a prompt and uploads are provided, the agent must **seamlessly merge** them into a single Module core while keeping **provenance badges** intact.\
- Before a module can be locked, the following checks must pass:\
  1) Citations present for non\uc0\u8209 original facts in the Module core and generated items; links resolve; **provenance badges** applied (Internal / Certified Core / Industry source / Cerply templates).\
  2) No made\uc0\u8209 up facts.\
  3) Reading level and length match target roles.\
  4) Duplicate or near\uc0\u8209 duplicate items removed; varied item shapes are present.\
  5) Basic accessibility checks pass (clear language, alt text for images, keyboard friendly order).\
  6) **Storage routing:** Internal content is stored only in the client\'92s Content Library; Certified Core and Industry source material are referenced (not duplicated) unless copying is explicitly allowed.\
  7) **Sign\uc0\u8209 posting:** The Content pane and source map clearly show which sections/items are Internal vs external (Certified Core / Industry source / Cerply templates).\
\
- Manager/Leader can Lock as Company Module (client private library). Only owners and client admins can edit. Others in the company can clone.\
- Certifier can Lock as Certified Candidate (enters review). When stamped, it becomes Certified Core (clients cannot edit the core; wraps allowed and must be labelled).\
- Consultant saves drafts to the client's Content Library and may **propose lock as a Company Module**.\
- A Manager must **approve/certify** the consultant's module before it becomes a locked Company Module. After approval, ownership moves to a client admin; the consultant keeps read\uc0\u8209 only history.\
- All locks create an immutable version. New edits create a new version.\
Locks apply to the Module core; generated items can be refreshed or re\uc0\u8209 generated from the locked core and will carry a link to the core version.\
\
1.6 Clone (fork) and merge\
- Any user with view rights can clone a module. The system records the parent/child link.\
- Owners may accept merge requests from child modules back into the parent.\
\
Acceptance tests (Build)\
- A user can create a Module (core) from prompt only, generate draft lessons, pass quality gates, and lock the core within one hour.\
- While the agent writes, Content is read\uc0\u8209 only, then becomes editable.\
- Certified Core cannot be edited by clients; wraps are allowed and labelled.\
- Lock creates an immutable version; later edits create a new version number.\
- A consultant\uc0\u8209 created module cannot be locked as a Company Module without an explicit manager approval/certification step.\
- When a Module is built from **both** prompt and uploads, the resulting Module core shows merged content with correct **provenance badges**, and Internal content is stored in the client\'92s Content Library.\
- 
\f1 \cf2 Core drafting uses a top model and passes a separate quality check by a second top model before lock; failed checks block lock and show flags to the user.
