------------------------------------\
2) Push \'97 delivery rules and nudges\
------------------------------------\
\
2.1 Targeting\
- Manager selects audience: teams, groups, or named people. Groups are created and managed in Cerply.\
\
2.1a Selection: Manager chooses a Module, selects the audience (teams, groups, or people), and sets **mandatory or recommended**, **start date**, **quiet hours**, and **daily cap** \'97 this creates a **Module assignment**.\
\
2.2 Scheduling and cadence\
- Send now or schedule one\uc0\u8209 off or a drip (for example, \'93two items per weekday\'94).\
- Prompt cap: at most 1\'962 mandatory prompts per day. Learners can choose to continue after mandatory items are done.\
- Quiet hours default: 20:00\'9608:00 local. Manager can override per module or audience.\
\
2.3 Variations and repeats\
- Each send creates varied items derived from the Module core. Learners should not see the same item wording twice.\
- Exact repeats are allowed only when the module has the tag Compliance Critical.\
\
2.4 Learner controls\
- Learners may mute recommended modules and unmute later. Mandatory modules cannot be muted.\
\
Acceptance tests (Push)\
- Manager can send to a group and see a delivery status within minutes.\
- Mandatory cap is enforced; learners can opt to continue.\
- Quiet hours suppress nudges during the default window unless overridden.\
- Compliance Critical modules may deliver exact repeats; other modules do not.\
\
------------------------------------\
3) Learn \'97 natural language interactions\
------------------------------------\
\
3.1 Message types a learner can send\
- Answer: a response to a quick check.\
- Help: \'93Help\'94, \'93Explain\'94, or similar \'97 returns a short hint or recap.\
- Challenge: \'93This is wrong\'94, \'93Out of date\'94, \'93Does not match policy\'94 \'97 flags the item for manager review and allows the learner to continue.\
- Progress: \'93How am I doing?\'94 \'97 returns a compact card.\
\
3.2 Progress card (Slack/Teams/web)\
- Shows: Current level (0\'9610 and phase), Streak (days), Next due (date/time), Actions: Continue, Review weak area.\
- When \'93Continue\'94 is pressed, the next item is sent at the right difficulty.\
- When \'93Review weak area\'94 is pressed, the next items focus on the weakest skills first.\
\
3.3 Feedback\
- Each answer returns the correct answer, a short reason, and a link to a lesson or source if needed.\
\
3.4 Spacing and difficulty\
- The engine adjusts difficulty from recent performance (correctness, speed, signs of doubt) and time since last practice.\
- The engine plans the next session time to strengthen memory.\
\
Acceptance tests (Learn)\
- A learner can complete a daily mandatory set, then choose to do more.\
- \'93How am I doing?\'94 returns the progress card with the right fields.\
- \'93Challenge\'94 flags the item and notifies the module owner for review.\
- Compliance Critical allows exact repeats; others deliver varied wording.\
\
------------------------------------\
4) Track \'97 dashboards and export\
------------------------------------\
\
4.1 Views\
- Team view: mastery by skill, time to first competence, active users, at\uc0\u8209 risk users, recent wins, stale modules.\
- Person view: current level, pace, weak areas, streaks, last session time.\
- Module view: core freshness (stale sections), version age, reach, answer rates in **Module assignments**, time on task, drop\uc0\u8209 offs, confusing items, too\u8209 easy items.\
\
4.2 Filters\
- Filter by team, role, date range, module, skill, tag (including Compliance Critical).\
\
4.3 Exports\
- Managers, Certifiers, and Admins can export a complete Module as a PDF. The PDF includes a watermark and version stamp and contains the Module core outline plus selected generated items (sample lessons/checks) **with provenance badges**. Learners cannot export anything.\
\
Acceptance tests (Track)\
- Each view loads under two seconds with realistic data volumes.\
- PDF export shows correct version lineage.\
- Deleting a learner removes personal data while leaving anonymous aggregates.\
\
------------------------------------\
5) Certified \'97 review and catalogue\
------------------------------------\
\
5.1 Submission\
- Any owner may submit a module as a Certified Candidate with sources and tags.\
\
5.2 Review\
- Reviewer checks: clarity, accuracy, relevance, sector fit, and sample items.\
- Example\uc0\u8209 only time goals: urgent takedown within 24 hours; standard review within five business days.\
\
5.3 Stamp and publish\
- On approval, the Module core becomes Certified Core and enters the catalogue with tags, sector, and level.\
- Clients can create **Module assignments** based on Certified Core and add a labelled wrap (for example, \'93Client Addendum\'94). Wraps must not change the Certified goals.\
\
5.4 Find and use\
- Search and filter by skill, sector, level, role, tag. Results show stamp details and version.\
\
Acceptance tests (Certified)\
- A Certified Candidate can be approved and becomes Certified Core with a visible stamp and version.\
- Client wraps are clearly labelled and cannot change Certified Core.\
\
------------------------------------\
6) Admin & Governance \'97 roles, rights, and rules\
------------------------------------\
\
- Learner: receive items; natural language interactions; no exports; no edits to content.\
- Manager/Leader: build by prompt/upload; edit Company Modules; **approve/certify consultant\uc0\u8209 created modules**; create Module assignments; track; export PDF; submit for Certified; wrap Certified Core (labelled).\
- Certifier: build; review; stamp; manage Certified Core and versions; no client data export beyond PDFs of modules.\
- Consultant: build; save drafts to the client's Content Library; **propose** lock as Company Module; cannot lock without manager approval; hand over ownership after approval; no access after handover except read\uc0\u8209 only history.\
- Company Admin: manage users, teams, groups, roles, defaults, quiet hours, content rules and filters, data regions.\
- Cerply Admin: 
\f1 \cf2 manage global catalogue, safety policies, platform settings, 
\f2\b model defaults and failover
\f1\b0 , and cost caps.
