13) Release notes anchors (for planning)\
------------------------------------\
- R1: Build (prompt\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 module, locks, versions), Push (cap, quiet hours), Learn (progress card), Track (dashboards), Certified (review/stamp), Admin (roles), PDF export.\
- R2: Directory sync, single sign\uc0\u8209 on, more item shapes, stronger accessibility tools.\
\
------------------------------------\
14) Models & orchestration\
------------------------------------\
\
What we use and why\
- We use real models for the agent. No pretend intelligence.\
- We route work to the right model: small and fast for chat and control; top model for drafting; second top model for a quality check.\
\
Routing rules\
- Build (outline, core drafting) \uc0\u8594  top model with citations.\
- Quality check (facts, citations) \uc0\u8594  different top model; flags block lock until fixed.\
- Chat and small edits \uc0\u8594  small fast model.\
- Push and Learn runtime decisions \uc0\u8594  small fast model with back-off if load is high.\
\
Safety and guard rails\
- Respect content rules: only allowed industry sources; blocked terms are enforced.\
- No exact repeats unless the Module is tagged Compliance Critical.\
- Personal data kept private; only anonymous patterns are used for long-term optimisation.\
\
Cost and speed\
- Default model choices aim for good speed and low cost in year one.\
- Cerply Admin can set caps, swap defaults, or fail over if a model is slow or down.\
\
Observability\
- We log model label, time, tokens, and estimated cost per job (no personal data).\
- Dashboards show latency and error rates so we can tune routing.\
\
Acceptance tests (Models)\
- Drafting runs on a top model and a second top model runs the quality check; failed checks block lock.\
- A Push and Learn message can still send when a top model is down (fallback to small fast model for routing decisions).\
- Model logs record label, time, tokens, and estimated cost for each job.\
\
End of FSD.\
}